# Copy to `.env` for local development (`.env` is gitignored).
# Production: set the same names in Vercel project Environment Variables (never `VITE_`).
# Server-only: NASA and Gemini keys must not be exposed to the browser bundle.
#
# Local serverless + Vite: `npm run dev:vercel` (uses `vercel dev --local` — no Vercel cloud login required).
# Reads this `.env` for `api/*` function env. `npm run dev` (Vite on :5173) does not serve `/api/*`.
# Optional: link a Vercel project for cloud env sync — `vercel link` then `vercel dev` without `--local`,
# or set VERCEL_TOKEN for non-interactive login when the network can reach vercel.com.
NASA_API_KEY=your_nasa_api_key_here
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
GEMINI_MODEL=your_gemini_model_here